From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmage22 <dmage22@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:07:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: fixes for protected launchers that decrypt code on
 demand

Squashed from Dmage22/FEX-D2 branch d2r/clean (Diablo II: Resurrected, Overwatch 2).
Tracks executable views of non-image sections, decides image views by MEM_IMAGE, asks the OS
about unknown executable pages, raises generated faults with hlt and the right exception code,
retries stale NoExec faults, carries PF/AF through context conversion when ntdll exports
__wine_arm64ec_extended_eflags, copies only decoded extents into the disk cache, restarts the
compiler at inaccessible pages instead of deadlocking on the invalidation lock, and decodes
0x67 MOVS/STOS and FS/GS selector loads in 64-bit mode.

Upstream: analysis in FEX-Emu/FEX#5328; no PR yet.
